{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"Snapshot success waits for the sink to close and for the FSM restore future to complete. The FSM worker reports completion only after `Restore` returns successfully, and the leader then checks transport error, response term, and success before registering the snapshot index. This explains the suspected early-acknowledgment path in source; crash durability and snapshot freshness remain separate questions.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > prepare_snapshot_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v2.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']: a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n for k in ('established_by','consumed_by'): f.pop(k,None)\nsources=[dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k) for i,f,a,b,k in [('src_install_snapshot','raft.go',1810,1953,'code_observation'),('src_fsm_restore','fsm.go',188,214,'code_observation'),('src_fsm_dispatch','fsm.go',237,264,'code_observation'),('src_fsm_restore_call','fsm.go',266,285,'code_observation'),('src_snapshot_contract','snapshot.go',15,67,'interface_statement'),('src_fsm_contract','fsm.go',15,49,'interface_statement'),('src_snapshot_open_send','replication.go',297,380,'code_observation')]]\nbrestore=dict(id='B_restore_fsm',primary_activity='A5',execution_owner='Raft runFSM goroutine',protocol_context='restoreFuture identifying one locally finalized snapshot by sink ID',trigger='restoreFuture arrives on fsmMutateCh',reads=['SnapshotStore.Open(req.ID) metadata and bytes'],writes=['FSM state through Restore','Worker lastIndex and lastTerm after Restore success'],external_effects=['Respond to restoreFuture with error or nil'],important_branches=['Open error responds with error','FSM Restore error responds with error','Successful restore sets worker index/term before respond(nil)'],async_boundaries=['fsmMutateCh from main Raft thread','Future error completion to waiting installSnapshot'],cross_activity_effects={'A3':'Completes restoration used to establish eligible snapshot state before receiver acknowledgment','A1':'Nil completion is a required predecessor of the snapshot success reply eventually registered as replication support'},source_ids=['src_fsm_restore','src_fsm_dispatch','src_fsm_restore_call','src_fsm_contract'],unknowns=['Injected FSM correctness is conditional on its interface contract; arbitrary implementation corruption is not ruled out.'])\ninstall=dict(id='B_install_snapshot',primary_activity='A3',execution_owner='Raft main thread installSnapshot handler',protocol_context='InstallSnapshotRequest with term, index/term, configuration and stream size',trigger='Incoming InstallSnapshot RPC',implementation_guards=['Supported snapshot version','Request term at least current term','Copy succeeds and byte count equals declared size','Sink.Close succeeds','Restore future returns nil'],reads=['Current term','Request metadata and snapshot stream','Snapshot sink and restore completion'],writes=['Term/role for higher-term request','Local snapshot','lastApplied and lastSnapshot','Latest and committed configuration'],durable_effects=['SnapshotSink.Close success is required, but physical durability depends on actual store'],external_effects=['Deferred stream drain followed by RPC response; Success set true only after restore and metadata updates'],important_branches=['Version, stale term, copy, size, close and restore errors cannot reach final Success=true','Shutdown during restore enqueue returns without success','Log cleanup errors are logged but do not prevent success'],async_boundaries=['Stream reader may block','Enqueues restoreFuture to runFSM and waits on Error','Deferred RPC reply after stream draining'],produces_fact_ids=['F_snapshot_installed'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Success provides the snapshot completion fact consumed by sender replication support registration','A4':'Installs snapshot configuration as latest and committed'},existing_protections=['Success is after actual restore completion rather than queue receipt','Shutdown future error does not masquerade as restore success'],source_ids=['src_install_snapshot','src_future_completion','src_snapshot_contract'],unknowns=['Stale but same/higher-term snapshot freshness and regression are not resolved by the completion ordering','Store crash durability and restart reconstruction are not reviewed','Ignored log cleanup errors need separate analysis; they do not imply missing FSM restoration'])\nsender=dict(id='B_snapshot_match',primary_activity='A1',execution_owner='Per-follower leader replication goroutine',protocol_context='Current followerReplication commitment pointer and selected snapshot metadata',trigger='Missing log fallback calls sendLatestSnapshot',reads=['SnapshotStore.List highest-index-first result','SnapshotStore.Open metadata and stream','InstallSnapshot transport response'],writes=['nextIndex=meta.Index+1 and commitment.match(peer.ID,meta.Index) after accepted success','Last contact and failure count'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_snapshot_installed'],important_branches=['List/open/transport errors return without match','Higher response term invokes handleStaleTerm and stops','Success=false adds no match','Success=true registers selected snapshot index and notifies waiting leader verification futures'],async_boundaries=['Synchronous InstallSnapshot transport call','commitment mutex and notification'],existing_protections=['Checks transport error before reading support','Rejects response term greater than request term','Uses sent snapshot index rather than any follower log hint'],source_ids=['src_snapshot_open_send','src_snapshot_match','src_commitment','src_snapshot_contract'],unknowns=['Response correlation is conditional on transport API; full transport and leadership generation lifecycle not mapped','Snapshot creation from committed history and freshness relative to follower applied state remain separate questions'])\nm['behaviors'] += [brestore,install,sender]\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F_snapshot_installed',meaning='For a successful response produced by installSnapshot, the supplied stream passed exact-size copy and sink Close, the FSM restore future returned nil, and receiver lastApplied, lastSnapshot and configurations were assigned from request metadata before reply. This is completion at that handler, not a guarantee of physical durability or request freshness.',identity={'request':'InstallSnapshot RPC and its response','snapshot':'Request LastLogIndex/LastLogTerm and newly created sink ID','receiver':'Receiving Raft instance'},validity_context='At successful receiver reply; subsequent state changes and restart are not covered.',representation=['InstallSnapshotResponse.Success','Request snapshot index/term/configuration','restoreFuture Error completion'],durability='Conditional on SnapshotStore and FSM contracts; acknowledgment itself is not a durable object.',recovery='Restart reconstruction not mapped.',source_ids=['src_install_snapshot','src_fsm_restore','src_fsm_restore_call','src_snapshot_open_send','src_snapshot_contract'],unknowns=['Request provenance and monotone snapshot freshness remain unproven','Log cleanup failure does not prevent success','Sender consumption depends on transport preserving request/reply correspondence']))\nf=next(x for x in m['facts'] if x['id']=='F_commit')\nf['unknowns']=['Snapshot success producer and restore completion are now mapped; actual store durability, snapshot provenance and leadership-context validity remain unproven.','Match report truth and legal configuration transitions remain obligations to investigate, not assumed facts']\nf['source_ids']+=['src_install_snapshot','src_snapshot_open_send','src_fsm_restore']\nfor cid,purpose,summary,ss in [('A3','Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation','Snapshot receiver completion and its restore wait are mapped.',['src_install_snapshot']),('A5','Decision application and consumption','FSM restore completion supports snapshot resynchronization; ordinary Apply path remains unmapped.',['src_fsm_restore','src_fsm_contract'])]:\n m['activities'].append(dict(class_id=cid,applicability='applicable',purpose=purpose,realization_summary=summary,source_ids=ss))\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n if s['entry_point']=='Raft.sendLatestSnapshot':\n  s.update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_snapshot_match','B_install_snapshot','B_restore_fsm'],reason='Mapped completion-to-match dependency. Sink close and actual FSM restore completion precede receiver success; sender checks error/term/success. Snapshot freshness, generation validity and crash recovery remain unresolved.',source_ids=['src_snapshot_open_send','src_install_snapshot','src_fsm_restore'])\nq=dict(question='Can the receiver successful snapshot acknowledgment counted by sendLatestSnapshot be produced merely on enqueue to the FSM, before snapshot finalization or successful FSM Restore completion?',importance='Snapshot acknowledgments contribute a follower match index to A1 commitment support. Premature success could let reported support precede reconstructed state. This question only concerns the completion boundary, not crash durability or legality/freshness of snapshot history.',source_ids=sorted(set(install['source_ids']+sender['source_ids']+brestore['source_ids']+['src_fsm_restore_call'])),participants=['Leader replication goroutine','Follower main Raft thread','Follower runFSM worker'],objects=['InstallSnapshot RPC','SnapshotSink','restoreFuture','Follower match index'],contexts=['Snapshot fallback with receiver-produced Success=true','Store/FSM methods obey documented contracts','Arbitrary finite delay of the restore worker'],event_paths=['sendLatestSnapshot -> installSnapshot copy and Close -> runFSM Restore -> restoreFuture nil -> receiver Success -> sender match'],activity_classes=['A1','A3','A5'],behavior_ids=['B_install_snapshot','B_snapshot_match'],fact_ids=['F_snapshot_installed'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_restore_fsm':'Actual asynchronous producer of nil restore completion; it waits for FSM Restore to return successfully.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['installSnapshot synchronously checks sink.Close then waits on future.Error before assigning success.','runFSM responds nil only after Restore returns nil and worker index/term updates.','The sender rejects transport errors, higher response terms and unsuccessful responses before match.'],unknowns=['Physical durability and restart outcomes depend on store implementations not examined here.','Freshness, leader prefix, and later invalidation are not established.','Log cleanup errors are intentionally nonfatal and not decided by this completion-order explanation.'],priority=2,trigger_rationale='The snapshot path asynchronously transfers work to the FSM but later contributes a match index. Followed the actual future producer to distinguish enqueue receipt from restoration completion.',disposition='explained_by_existing_mechanism',preferred_check='source_review')\nchanges={'F_commit':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['src_install_snapshot','src_fsm_restore','src_snapshot_open_send'],rationale='Replace the previously unread snapshot-producer gap with sourced completion ordering while retaining durability, provenance and context gaps. Conditional reported-support meaning is unchanged; this is an independent producer family and does not alter the pipeline access-order witness.'),'surface:Raft.sendLatestSnapshot':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['src_install_snapshot','src_fsm_restore','src_snapshot_open_send'],rationale='Expand the deferred snapshot surface into actual sender, receiver and FSM restore behaviors. No existing question depends on this surface for its local interface proposition.')}\njson.dump(m,open('map-snapshot.json','w'),indent=2)\np=dict(action='explained',map_path='map-snapshot.json',map_changes=changes,sources=sources,question=q,rationale='Source explanation closes only the early-acknowledgment suspicion: successful sink finalization and real restore completion precede receiver success, and the sender guards match registration. A delayed or failing restore cannot produce the counted successful acknowledgment through this code path. No execution Evidence or full snapshot correctness claim is created. Return to the frontier: next inspect configuration activation and retained voter matches, which can change eligibility directly; this is higher-value than executing already explicit restore waiting. Snapshot freshness remains another valuable direction requiring a legal sender/follower prefix, while network partial-decode consequences need a distinct fault witness.')\njson.dump(p,open('submission-snapshot-explained.json','w'),indent=2)\njsonschema.validate(p,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\njsonschema.validate(m,json.load(open('../product-schemas.json'))['ConsensusAuditSpec'])\nprint('Snapshot map and explanation schemas validated.')\nPY\npython3 prepare_snapshot_map.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
